  "body": "## What changed\n\nA 2D Chamfer or a Deburr generated with no warnings, but the post gate then refused it as a gouge. The program sim judged the bevel the op exists to cut against the model's sharp edge. This PR makes the op own its break, the issue's option 1. The bevel comes from the op's **stated** parameters, not from its moves.\n\n- **`cl::EdgeBreak`** (new, `crates/cl/src/cl/edge_break.rs`): a record of the break the op was asked to cut. It holds the edge as a polyline at its own height, the bevel depth at the edge, and the slope. `floor_at(x, y)` gives the cone swept along the edge, limited to the stated plan width. It is carried on `cl::Toolpath::breaks` and is empty for every other kind.\n- **Generators declare their breaks:**\n  - `machining2d::chamfer` declares the picked loops at `top_z`, with depth `width*tan(angle)` and slope `tan(angle)`.\n  - `finishing3d::deburr` declares its edge runs, with depth `drop` and slope `cot(half-angle)`.\n  - Neither reads the declaration back off the moves.\n- **Sim credit** (new, `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/edge_break.rs`, `credit_breaks`): this runs after `deviate`, from `simulate_document`. A gouge column inside a declared break's width, under a model top no higher than the edge, is re-judged against the bevel:\n  - Cut down to the bevel (within `DEV_TOL`): clean.\n  - Cut below the bevel: still a gouge, charged at its depth under the bevel.\n  - Rest is untouched.\n  - An edge nobody declared, or a boss standing above the edge, keeps the model's verdict.\n  - `deviate` and `deviate_field` are not touched, so this stays clear of #481's `wall_slack.rs`.\n- **Deburr skips steep edges** (generator fix, found while reproducing). The issue said the deburr's deeper gouge columns were link rapids. They were the vertical corner edges. A vertical cone riding a vertical edge, apex `drop` under each point, countersinks the corner down to the window floor. With the default window that is 9.8 mm on the 10 mm brick, a real gouge. The kernel now skips any edge that climbs steeper than the cone's flank, and says so in a path note.\n- **Persistence:** the cached path gets an additive `breaks` key (`project/break_dto.rs`). Absent means none, so an old cache is judged against the sharp model until it regenerates (stricter, never looser).\n- **Tilted (3+2) frames:** `TiltedFrame::world_path` translates the breaks when the frame is upright and drops them when it is tilted. A posed program is refused by the verdict anyway.\n- **Multi-setup programs:** when the program spans setups that hold the part differently, only the final frame's ops' breaks are credited.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/303-op-owns-its-break.md`.\n\n## Readings (upstream/main b2659dbe, brick 40x20x10, stock = brick, CM-0600-90)\n\n| Job | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2D Chamfer, kind defaults | `gouge: ... 624 cell(s), worst 0.74 mm` | gate clean, posts |\n| Deburr, kind defaults (w 0.5, window = model) | `gouge: ... 495 cell(s), worst 9.80 mm at (19.94, -9.81, z 0.20)`: the vertical-corner countersink | gate clean, posts (4 vertical edges skipped, with a note) |\n| Deburr, the issue's ride (w 2, tips z 6..8) | `gouge: ... 1544 cell(s), worst 3.80 mm` | gate clean, posts |\n| Default chamfer, moves lowered 0.3 mm | - | `gouge: ... worst 0.30 mm` |\n| Chamfer picks brick A, moves carried onto brick B | - | `gouge: ... worst 0.7x mm` |\n\n## Tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/edge_break_gate.rs` (new, 5 tests):\n  - `a_default_2d_chamfer_on_a_finished_brick_posts` (fails on main)\n  - `a_default_deburr_on_a_finished_brick_posts` (fails on main)\n  - `a_chamfer_ridden_deeper_than_its_stated_break_still_refuses`\n  - `a_chamfer_on_an_edge_it_was_not_asked_to_break_still_refuses`\n  - `the_declared_break_survives_save_and_load`\n- `crates/sim/tests/edge_break_credit.rs` (new, 5 tests):\n  - the declared chamfer is clean\n  - over-deep is charged exactly 0.3\n  - an undeclared edge keeps its full verdict\n  - a boss above the edge is never credited\n  - a sloped edge's bevel matches a brute-force swept cone\n- `crates/motion/tests/chamfer_circular.rs`: `the_chamfer_declares_the_break_it_was_asked_to_cut` (new).\n- `crates/app/tests/deburr_links.rs`: the #304 link test now rides a model with two blocks. The single brick, with its vertical edges skipped, is one run and has no link left to test.\n- `crates/motion/tests/deburr.rs`:\n  - `a_vertical_edge_is_skipped_out_loud_never_countersunk` (new).\n  - `convex_creases_all_ride_a_closed_box_breaks_every_edge` renamed to `..._every_level_edge`. The box's level creases ride and its 4 vertical corners are skipped with a note.\n  - `the_window_clips_along_the_edges_own_line` re-pinned on a sloped (1 in 2) rim, because the old curtain's vertical sides are now skipped.\n- Test-literal updates for the new `Toolpath` field, with no behaviour change: sim rapids/pose tests, motion `one_descent`, app `turning_rapids_tests`.\n- Gate results (debug):\n  - `cargo test --no-fail-fast -p camcraft-cl -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app`: 282 binaries, all green.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-cl -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Release `--ignored` lanes:\n  - all of `camcraft-sim`, plus app `operations`, `stock_sim_document` and `posting`: green.\n  - app `stock_engine_agreement`: its 2 known-red tests (#494) fail as they do on main. That suite calls `deviate` directly, not `simulate_document`, so this change does not reach it.\n- No golden changed. No chamfer or deburr goldens exist.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- GUI Deviate view, by eye. A real cut.\n- A chamfer on a 3+2 tilted frame: its breaks are dropped, and the posed verdict refuses it as before.\n- Deburr edges that are shallower than the flank but whose adjacent face rises above the edge (a bottom rim ridden from above). The window keeps the default off them. If one is ridden, the sim still convicts it, correctly.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Chamfer or Deburr on a finished part now posts: the program sim judges the op's declared edge break against its stated width and angle instead of the sharp model edge, while a deeper or undeclared break still refuses as a gouge; the deburr no longer rides vertical edges (it countersank the corners) and says so (#303)\n\nFixes #303\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
